  "answer": "### Short Answer\nYou are late in filing your annual income tax return if you have not submitted it by April 15 of the year following the taxable year. This deadline is established under Section 51(C)(1) of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Interpretation\nThe NIRC mandates that individual taxpayers must file their income tax returns by April 15 each year. If you have not filed your return by this date, you are considered late. This requirement applies to all individuals subject to income tax, including citizens and resident aliens.\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFiling late may result in penalties and interest on the unpaid tax due. It is advisable to file your return as soon as possible to minimize any additional charges. If you have missed the deadline, you should also consider consulting with a tax professional to understand your options for compliance and any potential penalties.",
